      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{2},$ calculate $\\text{Var}[-\\sqrt{2}X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[-\\sqrt{2}X] & ={(-\\sqrt{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
